※ The rule that catches an unread value inside a function, asked of a variable
※ the whole program can name.  Nothing reads what is written here, so writing it
※ cannot affect what the program does.
let counter: mut u8 = 1u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    counter ← 7u8
    3u8
